plained). Completed the mandatory single-node restart protocol: captured pre-restart boot_id and service health, issued `systemctl reboot`, confirmed connection drop/timeout, polled until reachable again, verified boot_id changed, and confirmed firewalld/nftables/sshd all recovered with the identical persisted configuration.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1 OS and existing firewalld/nftables state\",\"Added --permanent ssh and 8080/tcp to firewalld public zone\",\"Set public zone target to REJECT for persistent default-deny\",\"Removed pre-existing unrelated allowances (cockpit, dhcpv6-client) to satisfy 'reject unrelated inbound'\",\"Reloaded firewalld and verified runtime + permanent config match\",\"Inspected generated nftables ruleset to confirm allow-list (22,8080) then reject with icmpx admin-prohibited\",\"Ran live listener tests on 8080 (success) and 9999 (self-curl loopback artifact, explained as not proof of misconfig given single-node topology)\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id and firewalld/sshd health baseline\",\"Issued systemctl reboot on node1, confirmed disconnect, polled until node1 exec available again\",\"Verified changed boot_id, and re-verified firewalld state, persisted zone config, nftables rules, and sshd health post-restart\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Persistent firewall permits SSH and TCP 8080\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d107a6a41b744c99\",\"cmd-b39b793c55464edc\",\"cmd-7ef75988122f4e4d\"],\"summary\":\"firewall-cmd --permanent and --list-all show ssh service and 8080/tcp allowed; nftables filter_IN_public_allow chain accepts tcp dport 22 and 8080; config persisted to /etc/firewalld/zones/public.xml\"},{\"requirement\":\"Unrelated inbound rejected\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-b39b793c55464edc\",\"cmd-deed77eb98f64c31\"],\"summary\":\"Zone target set to REJECT (%%REJECT%%); nftables filter_IN_public chain falls through to 'reject with icmpx admin-prohibited' for anything not matching the allow chain; removed unrelated pre-existin